/* Deep lessons — Graph algorithms (graphs).
 *
 * The largest track here, and the one where a shallow lesson does the most
 * damage: a learner who has "seen BFS" but cannot recognise that a puzzle
 * with states is a graph has learned nothing usable.
 *
 * So this track spends its first stage on modelling — turning a problem into
 * a graph — and returns to that idea at stages 19 and 20, where the graph is
 * never given explicitly. The algorithms in between are taught in the order
 * their ideas depend on each other, not in order of fame.
 *
 * Original text and diagrams. Nothing copied from any source.
 */

import type { DeepLesson } from "../deep-lesson";

